                <pb facs="0517" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg503"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adams, Secretary of State, to Mr. Prince, United
                        States marshal.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1820-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 25,
                        1820</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of the 17th instant, which
                    informs me of the sentence pronounced upon Rosemaine and others, by the circuit
                    court of the United States for the district of Massachusetts, has been duly
                    received. From a full consideration of all the circumstances of the case, the
                    President declines interposing, and leaves them to the operation of the law.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN QUINCY ADAMS.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Prince</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marshal of the United States for the district of
                            Massachusetts.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
